      "text": [
        " \"مَا صَنَعْتُمْ بِصَاحِبِكُمْ\" قَالُوا دَفَنَّاهُ قَالَ \"لَوْ عَلِمْتُ مَا دَفَنَّاهُ مَعَ أَهْلِ اَلْإِسْلاَمِ تَرَكَ وُلْدَهُ يَتَكَفَّفُونَ اَلنَّاسَ\" \"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5427 - Harun ibn Muslim narrated from Masadah ibn Ṣadaqah Al-Rabii from Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) from his father, Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as), who said:\n\"A man from the Ansar passed away, leaving behind young children. He had six slaves and no wealth other than them. At the time of his death, he freed all of them.\nWhen the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) was informed of this, He (sw) said:\n'What did you do with your companion?'\nThey replied: 'We buried him.'\nProphet (sw) said: 'Had I known before, I would not have allowed him to be buried among the Muslims. He (the deceased) left his children to beg from the people.'\""
        ]
      }
    },
